# scripts/security/external-agents.local
#
# User LaunchAgents deliberately managed outside this flake. The macOS
# security audit lists these as MANUAL ("verify against the managing repo")
# instead of undeclared-persistence WARN. The re-registration helper uses the
# same file as its only local allow-list.
#
# One exact plist filename per line. Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored.
# A name matches both `<name>.plist` and `<name>.plist.disabled` in the audit.
# A LaunchAgent under the configured prefix that is NOT listed here still
# WARNs. The relaunch helper only processes the listed `.plist` names.
#
# Optional relaunch directives are comments with the following exact forms:
# relaunch-prefix=com.example.
# relaunch-lock-path=/absolute/path/to/shared.lock
# relaunch-lock-label=com.example.import
# relaunch-lock-label=com.example.verify
# These directives are parsed as data; the file is never sourced as shell.
#
# Copy to scripts/security/external-agents.local (gitignored) and edit.
#
# relaunch-prefix=com.example.
# relaunch-lock-path=/path/to/shared.lock
# relaunch-lock-label=com.example.import
# com.example.daily-thing.plist
# com.example.backup.plist
